			<div class="content" id="post-content-855000">
									

<p>*soapbox*</p>
<p>If you're thinking of a humanoid SCP as a character, I can safely say it's not going to go well, no matter what you do—because you're fundamentally thinking of it the wrong way. Evidence: Whiny telepath ("Saint"), is dying, but 231 (110-Montauk) isn't. Looking at my attempts: baleeted-795 and baleeted-770 were erased, because they were characters with SCP-like effects. However, the asian girl in 466 is just a host, and that article is at a comfortable +5. Some of the older character-SCPs are getting away with it, but that's because herp derp cant criticize teh classix lol. Yet, 132 isn't looking so good…</p>
<p>TL;DR: SCP characters get deleted.</p>

