			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-855159">
									

<p>Very, very meh to me. It seems like a lot of focus is put on how she consumes things. When I think a human SCP with kind of freaky powers, I don't think of how they eat. I think of how it affects them. From the interview, it seems like she doesn't want to hurt people and she views herself as demonic, but the rest of the article is really about how she eats things. I don't want to think 'Wow, I want to be this person.' I want to think 'I never want to be this person, let alone be near them.'</p>
<p>I've downvoted the article for now, but I think that you MIGHT be able to save this with a good old fashioned rewrite. Human SCPs are hard to write, honestly, and if this is your first attempt I'd say try again but with something that isn't human. Take a waffleiron and make it weird or something.</p>

